nditional \u2014 the render is a plain `cat` of the whole body, so EVERY `launch`/`run` invocation fails regardless of which cells apply. bunker-qa.sh mtime 2026-10-19 14:42 (the ui-probe/BUNKER_QA_UI_PORTS patch) is the delta that introduced it; the 2026-10-17 dogfood run's battery (agent e68a175d) predates it and succeeded. Every dogfood lane's install leg and every QA-lane battery is blocked until this is fixed.\n\nSIDE EFFECT (agent leak): the abort happens AFTER the spawn, and the abort path does not destroy the agent \u2014 1dd1f7eb stayed running (bunker list showed it live, 0 B disk) until destroyed by hand ~8 minutes later in this run (`bunker destroy 1dd1f7eb --server bunker-mvp` \u2192 'Agent 1dd1f7eb destroyed.'). Repeated ticks therefore accumulate orphan agents until the ~4h TTL reaps them.\n\nWHAT THIS RUN DID INSTEAD (so the row's cost is explicit): the install leg was driven by hand on the same live host per the skill's generic ephemeral procedure \u2014 fresh agent df-tj-1019 on bunker-mvp, documented https clone (2.08s, rc=0, HEAD 2177a3cf), documented `./install.sh` (1.09s, rc=0), documented smokes (--version 1.3.0 rc=0; firewall bridge block builtin-rm-rf-root; landlock probe FULL/ABI 4), delta smoke of the TJ-DF-046/047 fix (plain-allow egress tier kernel-denied EPERM with the APPLIED banner, allowlist honored, three named-cause degrade arms), agent destroyed rc=0.\n\nFIX DIRECTION: escape the body's controller-side references (`\\$UI_PORTS`, `\\${BUNKER_QA_UI_PORTS:-}`) exactly as :2424/:2436 already do; add a cheap post-render guard that refuses to spawn when the generated script is 0 bytes; destroy the agent on the abort path. Regression: render the battery in a scratch run and assert `wc -c` > 0.\n\nACCEPTANCE CRITERIA: `BUNKER_QA_SERVER=<live-host> bunker-qa.sh launch <repo>` either ships a non-empty battery (launch cell emitted) or aborts BEFORE spawning; no agent from a failed launch remains in `bunker list` 90s+ after the abort; a unit/