dev host) \u2192 correct: FULL/ABI 8 \u2192 \"fs tier CAN engage and net (egress) tier CAN engage (Landlock ABI 8 >= 4; opt in with TERMINAL_JAIL_LANDLOCK_NET=1)\", and the run-time behavior matches (net tier APPLIED, kernel EPERM in the same session). Two fresh installs (dev host ABI 8, bunker agent ABI 4) printed the correct arm, so the defect is specifically the absent-probe path.\n\nMECHANISM (install.sh, read the bytes): the summary block initialises from a variable it does not own \u2014\n  install.sh:1542   LL_SUMMARY_OUT=\"${TIER_FULL_OUT:-}\"\n  install.sh:1543   if [ -n \"$SCRIPT_DIR\" ] && [ -f \"$SCRIPT_DIR/scripts/landlock-capability-probe.py\" ] \u2026 \u2192 runs the landlock probe FRESH (1549) and echoes it\n`TIER_FULL_OUT` is (re)set by every `run_tier_probe` call (install.sh:1455 reset, :1466 set) and the LAST advisory-path call is the pidns probe (install.sh:1504) \u2014 never the landlock probe, which no `run_tier_probe` call reaches. So with the landlock probe absent (the file-existence guard at 1543 short-circuits) LL_SUMMARY_OUT still carries the PIDNS probe's `FULL` output: LL_VERDICT becomes FULL (1562), the ABI grep finds no \"ABI version (max supported)\" line so LL_ABI is forced to 0 (1569-1572), and the ABI<4 branch (1576) prints the fabricated \"fs tier CAN engage; net \u2026 ABI 0\" line. The UNKNOWN branch (1580-1581) is therefore dead code on any source that still runs the other probes.\n\nWHY IT MATTERS: the fix's whole purpose is an HONEST first-contact ceiling report; here it reports a tier ceiling and a kernel ABI it never measured, on the exact path (probe missing) where the docs promise it will say `unknown`. A user on such a source is told the fs tier can engage by an install that never classified Landlock.\n\nREACHABILITY: any install source that lacks scripts/landlock-capability-probe.py but keeps the other probes \u2014 a partial/trimmed source copy, or a future release tarball that omits scripts/ (release assets are not published yet; the git-clone path always has it). Note the existing red-proven installer cells in plugin/test_tjdf047_plain_allow_degrade.py evidently do not reproduce this shape: they must stub or remove the probe in a way that also prevents the pidns probe from leaving FULL in TIER_FULL_OUT.\n\nFIX DIRECTION: initialise LL_SUMMARY_OUT=\"\" instead of seeding it from TIER_FULL_OUT (the variable belongs to the tier-probe helper), or route the landlock probe through run_tier_probe like its siblings; keep the existing UNKNOWN wording. Add a fixture cell = scratch checkout with the landlock probe deleted AND the pidns probe present \u2192 expect the `unknown` line.\n\nACCEPTANCE CRITERIA: on an install source with scripts/landlock-capability-probe.py absent, `./install.sh` prints exactly the documented `unknown` line (no ABI number, no per-tier CAN/CANNOT claim) and still exits 0; the three other arms keep their current wording.", "status": "complete", "title": "[P2] installer containment-ceiling summary (TJ-DF-047) prints a FABRICATED arm when the landlock probe is absent: LL_SUMMARY_OUT seeded from the pidns probe's TIER_FULL_OUT -> 'fs tier CAN engage; net CANNOT (Landlock ABI 0 < 4)' instead of the documented 'unknown'", "updated_at": "2026-10-20T01:52:35+00:00", "detail": {"fingerprint": "45734a86295fc619ba6d0f918d32c3a922d446a5e76491432969966cf421f133"}, "worker_status": "complete", "completed_at": "2026-10-20T12:28:45Z", "commit_hash": "3683bec", "guard_result": "PASS", "worker_summary": "Foreman-direct mechanical fix: install.sh initializes LL_SUMMARY_OUT empty. Verified probe-absent scratch install rc=0 prints documented unknown arm with no ABI 0; plugin/test_install.py 97 passed/1 skipped; exact-head CI 39421330597 success; judge artifact unavailable after task-complete timeout.", "foreman_note": "Closed verification-only after live acceptance checks; GitReins task state flipped complete but no verdict artifact survived the timeout."}
