net-loader.py\n  $ TERMINAL_JAIL_LANDLOCK_NET=1 /tmp/df-tj-1019/prefix/terminal-jail /usr/bin/python3 -c '<connect 9999 code>'\n  terminal-jail: WARNING: Landlock network (egress) tier not applied (the payload cannot read /tmp/df-tj-1019/prefix/../lib/terminal-jail/landlock-net-loader.py in the launch that would run it); commands run with network egress unchanged — …\n  CONNECTED ok data=b'pong\\n'   (payload ran unchanged, cause named — correct)\n  (the same leg is reproduced on a fresh bunker box: HOME-installed tree, cause worded \"landlock-net-loader.py is not reachable by the launch's payload uid (a parent … lacks o+x — e.g. a 0700/0750 home)\")\n\nMECHANISM (two attach paths, two different checks):\n  - plain-allow path: standalone/terminal-jail:1046-1068 `_tj_egress_tier_decide` probes readability UNDER the launch it is about to run (`\"$@\" test -r \"$LANDLOCK_NET_LOADER\"`) and calls `_tj_egress_degrade` with the cause on every non-attach outcome — this is the half TJ-DF-046/047 fixed.\n  - modify path: the tail is composed INSIDE the engine before the wrapper ever sees it — plugin/terminal_jail/interruptor/decider.py:76 `_LANDLOCK_NET_TAIL = landlock_net_sandbox_prefix()` spliced by `_wrap_payload` (:79), whose reachability gate is plugin/terminal_jail/interruptor/landlock_net.py:727 `if not _world_traversable(loader)` — and `_world_traversable` (def plugin/terminal_jail/interruptor/landlock.py:1201) walks ONLY the ancestor directories' `S_IXOTH`, never the loader file's own read bits. A loader that is path-traversable but unreadable by the payload uid therefore passes, gets spliced into the rewrite, and standalone/terminal-jail:1271+ execs the already-composed rewrite with no reachability preflight of its own.\n\nWHY THE STATE IS REACHABLE, NOT A LAB CURIOSITY: any install whose loader keeps a path the payload uid can traverse but loses the file's read bit — a loader owned by another uid with 0600 (split-user or root-owned install run by a user), a tightened umask/ACL, a packaging step that drops modes. The uid-mapped arm is already handled (landlock_net.py:1058 branch, `--here` semantics), so this is the remaining hole in the same contract.\n\nFIX DIRECTION: in `sandbox_prefix()` test the loader's OWN readability for the launch uid (e.g. `os.access`/mode & 0o444 after the traversal walk) in addition to `_world_traversable`, and on failure return the empty tail + the existing `_degrade(...)` wording, so the payload runs unchanged with one named-cause line — the same posture the fs tier uses. Keep the plain-allow path's wording as-is (it is already correct).\n\nACCEPTANCE CRITERIA: with the net tier enabled and the net loader chmod 000, an auto-sandbox-shaped command (a script payload) still RUNS (rc from the payload, not 2) and stderr carries exactly one `WARNING: Landlock network (egress) tier not applied (<cause>)` line naming the unreadable loader; no raw `python3: can't open file … [Errno 13]` reaches the user.","status":"pending","title":"[P2] auto-sandbox (modify) path splices the net loader without a readability preflight: a loader unreadable by the payload uid passes _world_traversable (ancestor o+x only), so the rewrite dies with a raw python Errno 13 + rc=2 and NO named-cause line, while the plain-allow path degrades loudly on the identical state","updated_at":"2026-10-20T20:40:00Z","detail":{"fingerprint":"ff09c9c6a23200dd60a8b03bc047efc953119b7169a52ed20d21f6cdca34e9fe"},"worker_status":"failed-dispatch","worktree":"/home/kara/worktrees/terminal-jail-TJ-DF-050","branch":"wt/TJ-DF-050","foreman_note":"Two worker dispatches in tick terminal-jail-foreman-2026-10-20-20-07-17 produced zero file writes and no commit: glm-5.3-flash@zai-glm-default read-only loop stopped after 20 minutes; step-3.7-flash@stepfun exited with clean worktree. Row remains pending for a later tick; no code was implemented or judged."}
